# C3REAL — is the DECLARED C3 target learnable at all?

Workspace `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-coalgen-ws`. Interpreter
`/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover/.venv/bin/python` only. **Never modify**
`/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover` or its `.venv`. Change nothing sealed.
**Hard cap: 3 python processes, `nice -n 15`, all BLAS threads = 1, peak RSS under 5 GB.**
Print a peak-RSS line. Hold at most one anchor's rows in memory.

## Why, and why it is overdue

`C1REAL` and `C2REAL` have tested route 1 and route 2 for learnability against their declared
targets. **Route 3 has never been tested at all.** It was queued at 10:03 with a trigger that
was not honoured; this is that job.

The declared C3 target is the set-level interaction residual
`Psi_A = Delta F(A) - sum_{i in A} d_i`, learned by a **set-conditioned scalar interaction
head** `Psi_hat(Z, a0, A, a_A)`: permutation-invariant over `A`, anchored
`Psi_hat(empty) = Psi_hat({u}) = 0`, trained on `Psi_A / kappa` over the coalition support of
the bounded catalogue (contract v1 §C2). Sealed head literals: hidden `(64, 64)`, relu,
lr `1.0e-3`, Adam `(0.9, 0.999)`.

**Two structural facts must be reported before any fit statistic, because they bound what the
statistic can mean:**
- `Psi` is **identically zero on singletons by construction**, so any coalition-support set
  dominated by `|A| = 1` makes the target trivially predictable and the fit meaningless.
  **Report the coalition-size distribution of your training support first.**
- The set-conditioned head sees `q1_state` and `q2_state` per member
  (`_route_state` returns `(*row.q1_state, *row.q2_state)` for C3), so the Q1 schema defects
  propagate into it. `C1REAL` on the sealed 16-slot v1 schema found held-out top-1 at the
  constant floor; **`C1REALV2` on the repaired `mcrl-v025-stagec-q1-action-v2` schema
  (effective dimension 14, elevation added, off-axis repaired) moved top-1 from `0.1711` to
  `0.3381` and level `R^2` from `-0.2724` to `+0.0379`.** So a v1-schema result for C3 is not
  a final verdict either.

## What to do

**Run it on the repaired schema (v2) as the primary, and on v1 as a stated secondary**, so the
schema's effect on route 3 is visible rather than inferred. If time permits only one, run v2 and
say so.

Mirror `C1-DECLARED-TARGET-LEARNABILITY-V2-2026-09-10.md` (in `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws`) in
construction, evidence labelling and reporting shape. Read it first. Deviate only where C3
genuinely differs, and say where and why.

1. **Rows.** Exact-path coalition rows with the exact `Psi_A`. Set
   `PILOT_PRIMITIVE_SOURCE_FALLBACK = False` on the **imported module object in-process** — do
   not edit the file; assert byte-identity before and after. State the anchor count and the
   measured seconds per anchor.
2. **Verification before fitting.** Report the decomposition identity residual, and confirm
   `Psi` is exactly zero on every singleton in your support.
3. **Held-out protocol.** Leave-one-anchor-out **and** leave-one-world-out. Report level `R^2`,
   within-group pairwise ordering, and top-1 argmax agreement over the coalition candidates,
   each with an anchor-bootstrap interval at the same replicate count `C1REAL` used.
4. **References.** The sealed `(64,64)` head; a linear model; a **constant predictor** (report
   its top-1 explicitly — for C1 the constant floor `0.1716` against the head's `0.1711` is what
   produced the verdict); and a **high-capacity** model on the same inputs.
5. **Architectural versus informational.** If the sealed head underperforms, widen it (2-3
   widths) and report the best achievable fit of any function of the same inputs. **If a
   high-capacity model on the same inputs also fails, the ceiling is informational, not
   architectural — say so plainly and quantify it.**
6. **Permutation invariance.** Verify the head's declared invariance over `A` empirically, and
   report any violation. A head that is not invariant is not the declared object.

## Rules

- Separate **verified by running code**, **derived on paper**, **inferred**.
- **Loss values are never evidence about EE. This job makes no EE claim.** It reports predictive
  quality against a declared target.
- No production training, no policy run, no acceptance test.
- If the support is dominated by singletons or pairs, say so and state what that does to the
  interpretation, rather than reporting a strong fit without the caveat.

Write to `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-coalgen-ws/C3-DECLARED-TARGET-LEARNABILITY-2026-09-10.md`, first
