## Answer

[RUN] On the same 37 modeled exact-path anchors, changing Q1 from the defective
16-slot v1 representation to `mcrl-v025-stagec-q1-action-v2` changes the sealed
width-8 head's LOAO top-1 accuracy from `0.1711` to `0.3381`, a gain of
`+0.1670`; the unchanged constant floor is `0.1716`. Its raw held-out level
`R²` changes from `−0.2724` to `0.0379`, a gain of `+0.3102`. LOAO ordering
changes from `0.5889` to `0.7310`, a gain of `+0.1421`.

[INFERRED] Under the reading fixed before the run, these are material movements.
The result therefore supports **“the v1 verdict was an artefact of the defective
schema.”** It does not support the first reading that the ceiling is really
informational. This conclusion is about the v1 learnability verdict, not EE and
not production readiness.

## Evidence labels and scope

- `[RUN]` means verified by running the required interpreter against the current
  code and data.
- `[DERIVED]` means arithmetic or algebra applied to the run outputs and declared
  definitions.
- `[INFERRED]` is the interpretation required by the fixed reading.

[RUN] No production training, policy run, acceptance test, or EE endpoint ran.
Loss values are not used as EE evidence. This job makes no EE claim. No sealed
constant, threshold, sign, seed, horizon, price, guard, acceptance rule, control
law, manifest, or optimizer setting was changed.

