## Repaired-coordinate permutation importance

[RUN] Importance uses the high-capacity LOWO model and the unchanged v1 method:
globally permute one coordinate inside each held-out world fold, then report the
drop from baseline (`R² = −0.09024`, ordering `0.67989`, top-1 `0.28243`). Both
repaired coordinates carry substantial held-out signal.

| v2 slot | feature | Δ`R²` | Δordering | Δtop-1 | permuted `R²` | permuted order | permuted top-1 |
|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 5 | repaired `off_axis_angle` | `0.0943` | `0.0964` | `0.0770` | `−0.1846` | `0.5834` | `0.2054` |
| 6 | `focal_link_elevation` | `0.1909` | `0.1414` | `0.1381` | `−0.2811` | `0.5385` | `0.1443` |

[INFERRED] The repaired coordinates are not inert. Elevation is the stronger of
the two under all three permutation metrics, and each independently removes a
large part of the flexible model's held-out ordering/top-1 signal when broken.

## Rank, condition number, and effective dimension

[RUN] On the 36,360 modeled rows, using the same raw physical-unit convention as
the schema census, the full 15-column matrix has rank `14` and infinite condition
number because `missing_incumbent` is exactly zero. Dropping that documented
structural coordinate gives rank `14` and condition number `1.893761e4`.
Therefore the schema-defined effective dimension is `[DERIVED] 15 − 1 = 14`,
matching the full-corpus census in rank, full-condition class, and effective
dimension.

[RUN] There is an additional panel-specific fact that the earlier v1 report did
not audit: `nominal_required_power_over_cap` is exactly `1.0` on every one of
these 36,360 exact-path rows (it is also exactly `1.0` in the corresponding v1
panel). If “effective dimension on these rows” means the number of empirically
varying coordinates rather than the schema/census definition, the answer is
`13`; dropping both empirical constants gives rank `13` and condition number
`1.893723e4`, and the mean-centered full matrix has rank `13`. The broader
176,223-row census varies required power and therefore has 14 varying
coordinates. This sample-specific constancy is not caused by v2 and does not
alter the paired v1/v2 result, but it prevents claiming that every
subset-conditioned census number matches exactly.

