All committed values above were evaluated on the real `field="realised"` endpoint at **48 boundaries**. The numerator caps each user's integrated bits at **1,504,000,000 bits** before pooling; loss values are not used anywhere as EE evidence.

## Derived on paper

- The reported per-user numerator cap is `50,000,000 bit/s × (47 × 0.640 s) = 1,504,000,000 bits`.
- Exact Ψ is already normalized by κ in `_exact_interactions`, matching the learned Q1/Q2 and interaction score units. Singleton/empty exact interaction is zero by the decomposition; learned interaction is gated off for those same context-less rows.
- A top-two pair is called within one ULP when its absolute score gap is no greater than `max(ulp(top), ulp(second))`. This diagnostic does not relabel such a pair as mathematically equal; exact equality is recorded separately.

## Inferred from the measurements

- Context gating is the majority-row condition (79.164% None); this establishes coverage, not causal quality of either head.
- Learned Ψ flips more matched decisions than exact Ψ, supporting learned-head distortion rather than structural unreachability on this anchor sample.
- Exact Ψ crosses the learned additive margin at least once, falsifying structural/additive impossibility on this sample.
- Strict final-ranking tie-break flips account for 0 exact and 0 learned changes; the remaining changes are genuine score separations under the stated floating-point computation.

